---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="How to Use">
  <h1 class="text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight">How to use Kalorec</h1>
  <ol class="mt-4 list-decimal space-y-3 pl-5 text-zinc-700 dark:text-zinc-300">
    <li>Log in with GitHub.</li>
    <li>Pick a private source repo in Settings — that's where your recipes will live.</li>
    <li>Pick a different public sharing repo in Settings. Kalorec puts published copies there, and your profile link uses that repo.</li>
    <li>Add a recipe: type it in by hand, or paste a link to import it automatically.</li>
    <li>Check "Publish a copy on my public Kalorec profile" for recipes you want visitors to see, then copy your share link from Settings.</li>
    <li>Unpublishing removes the current public copy. GitHub history and copies made while it was public can persist. Recipes once stored in a public source repo can remain exposed in that repo's history.</li>
    <li>Browse a shared profile and click "Add to my recipes" to copy someone else's public recipe into your own repo.</li>
  </ol>
</Layout>
